# Every text file is LF in the repository and in every checkout, whatever the
# contributor's core.autocrlf says. DVC hashes files byte for byte, so a Windows
# checkout with CRLF endings makes every Python dependency in dvc.lock look
# changed, and `dvc repro` would rebuild the whole pipeline.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Pipeline outputs committed to Git (`cache: false` in dvc.yaml) are recorded in
# dvc.lock by their exact bytes, so Git must not touch their line endings.
# The CSVs are written by the csv module, which ends rows with CRLF everywhere.
metrics.json -text
reports/metrics/** -text
reports/data-validation/** -text
